WHY THE FLEET CANNOT SEE IT -- and this is the third confirmed sighting

COMPILE IS A PARSE CHECK. It asks whether emitted text PARSES, never whether it
MEANS anything. The ledger now has three sightings of the same blind spot, each
found a different way:

  1. probeNameResolve  -- the scaffold count compiled a body whose condition was
     `zzNotARule1() AND zzNotARule2();`, two names that are not rules and never
     will be.
  2. litToMissing      -- the odometer counted break GREEN while its emission
     called litTo(), which the substrate had not implemented.
  3. THIS ROW          -- the odometer counts DEFINing and tokenize GREEN while
     their emissions match literals that do not occur.

Each is one rung further from the text and one rung closer to meaning, and none
of the three is visible in a count. The instruments are honest about what they
measure; NONE OF THEM MEASURES CAPABILITY, and 19/58 must never be cited as
though it did.

⚠ SO TWO OF THE ODOMETER'S 19 ARE FALSE GREENS. The number is not withdrawn --
it is correct about what it measures -- but any plan that reads 19 as "19 rules
